\ tests/native/kernel-slit.4 - S" in a definition, laid inline by the
\ native compiler (Iteration 666): the bytes jumped over - by two bytes
\ of jmp up to 127, by five from 128 - and the address by a rip-relative
\ lea. Lengths 0 1 127 128 200; two in one word; in IF and ELSE; a word
\ small enough to be inlined, copied into others, and EXECUTEd; the
\ address's own bytes checked; the depth after. Native, CV8-asm and CV8-C
\ print the same.
: L0 S" " ;   : L1 S" x" ;
: L127 S" abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvw" ;
: L128 S" ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWX" ;
: L200 S" 01234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789" ;
: SUM ( c-addr u --- n )  0 SWAP 0 ?DO OVER I + C@ + LOOP SWAP DROP ;
: SHOW ( c-addr u --- )  DUP . 2DUP SUM . 8 MIN TYPE CR ;
L0 SHOW  L1 SHOW  L127 SHOW  L128 SHOW  L200 SHOW  DEPTH . CR
: TWO ( --- )  S" first" TYPE SPACE S" second" TYPE CR ;
TWO DEPTH . CR
: PICKS ( f --- )  IF S" yes" ELSE S" no" THEN TYPE CR ;
-1 PICKS  0 PICKS  DEPTH . CR
: HI S" hi" ;
: USE ( --- )  HI TYPE  1 HI ROT . TYPE  HI SWAP DROP . CR ;
USE  ' HI EXECUTE TYPE CR  DEPTH . CR
: MID ( --- n )  3 S" abcdef" DROP 2 + C@ + ;
MID . CR
\ A word whose body begins with a one-byte literal, and is not inlined
\ (it calls TYPE): its first bytes must not read as the inline marker,
\ jmp +1 and a length - they did, at first, and its callers copied 33
\ bytes of it for code (666)
: BANG ( --- )  S" !" TYPE ;
: USE-BANG ( --- )  BANG BANG CR ;
USE-BANG  DEPTH . CR
.( end) CR   \ the last line: verify's native_cmp wants it (656)
BYE
